\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Where shall my wondering soul begin?
\par How shall I all to heaven aspire?
\par A slave redeemed from death and sin,
\par A  brand plucked from eternal fire,
\par How shall I equal triumphs raise,
\par Or sing my great Deliverer's praise?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O how shall I the goodness tell,
\par Father, which Thou to me hast showed?
\par That I, a child of wrath and hell,
\par I should be called a child of God,
\par Should know, should feel my sins forgiven,
\par Blest with this antepast of heaven!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And shall I sight my Father's love?
\par Or basely fear His gifts to own?
\par Unmindful of His favours prove?
\par Shall I, the hallowed Cross to shun,
\par Refuse His righteousness to impart,
\par By hiding it within my heart?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Outcasts of men, to you I call,
\par Harlots, and publicans, and thieves!
\par He spreads His arms to embrace you all;
\par Sinners alone His grace receives:
\par No need of Him the righteous have;
\par He came the lost to seek and save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Come, O my guilty brethren, come,
\par Groaning beneath your load of sin!
\par His bleeding heart shall make you room,
\par His open side shall take you in;
\par He calls you now, invites you home:
\par Come, O my guilty brethren, come!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

